notes[1]{created_at,author,text,edited_at}:
  "2026-11-07T17:19:05.634Z","harness:claude-code","Scoping measurements (2026-11-07, built CLI 2026.11.7 plus this batch's refusal-listing change), taken before deciding whether this item could join the CLI option-contract batch. It was held out because the help half regresses token cost.\n\nAcceptance on the built CLI: update accepts every reserved host flag except the six read-output controls, which it refuses with \"Universal output controls apply only to read commands; update is not a read surface\" (code command_failed). get and list accept all of them. --expect-hash parses on every command. So per-command availability is: all reserved host flags, minus read-output controls unless resolveReadOutputSurface(command) is defined, minus any flag the command declares itself (close and list own --author; every core table already carries --output-format as an inherited row).\n\nCost: pm help close --json is 6,494 bytes today. The extension inherited_options rows (HelpOptionSummary, 12 fields each) cost about 260 bytes per row, so about 16 core rows add about 4.2 KB (+65%) to every per-command help JSON call. pm contracts --command close --flags-only --json rows cost about 110 bytes each, so about +1.8 KB. The multi-command pm contracts --flags-only --json listing is bounded at a 4,500-token default budget and shows 11 of 162 commands. Adding about 16 rows per core command there would push commands out of the default page, so the listing should stay unchanged.\n\nProposed design: (1) publish inherited_flags only on command-scoped reads (includeSemanticMetadata in buildCommandFlagSurface, src/sdk/cli-contracts/runtime-contracts.ts), derived from RESERVED_EXTENSION_HOST_FLAGS through a shared row builder with resolveExtensionCommandInheritedFlagContracts; (2) for help JSON, either a compact inherited row shape (flags, owner, value_name only) or a pointer to the contracts rows, which needs a ruling because extension commands already emit full rows; (3) the AC spec invokes every listed row on get and update.","2026-11-07T17:24:38.891Z"
body: ""
